## Context

The arena measured (model @effort) identities on WHOLE tickets — each
leg bundles orchestrator + coder + reviewer work in one wallclock. The
harness can do better: route PER TASK LEVEL within a piece of work and
optimize on the capability/effort scale (AGENTS.md profiles: cheap/
standard/strong/frontier x economy/standard/intensive). The tournament
data cannot answer "cheap triage + strong judgment" mixes.

## Scope

- Design a task-level variant of the instrument: decompose a ticket into
  routed steps (search/extraction -> cheap; implementation -> mid;
  judgment/verification -> strong), measure the mix vs the bundled
  arms on the same tickets.
- Compare: best bundled arm vs best routed mix at equal total cost.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Task-level routing design pre-registered (concept note sect. 8 sibling)
- [ ] One cycle comparing bundled vs routed on the arena sample
- [ ] Verdict: does task-level routing beat identity routing, and where
